cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use AnthroSim in research, cite the released software version and preserve the exact source revision used for the experiment."
title: "AnthroSim"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Datengu"
version: "0.2.0"
date-released: 2026-08-24
repository-code: "https://github.com/Datengu/anthrosim"
url: "https://github.com/Datengu/anthrosim"
license: "Apache-2.0"
keywords:
  - agent-based simulation
  - anthropology
  - archaeology
  - reproducibility
  - demography
  - migration
abstract: >-
  AnthroSim is a reproducible agent-based simulation framework for deterministic
  demography, resource-constrained household migration, kinship, and
  evidence-grounded spatial experiments under explicit model assumptions.
  Version 0.2.0 is the audited M8 evidence-grounded spatial experiment baseline,
  building on the deterministic synthetic v0.1 engine. Later capabilities on
  unreleased main are not part of the v0.2.0 citation baseline. AnthroSim is not
  an empirically validated model of human prehistory.
